-- title:
--   Base change of a semilinear automorphism to the geometric fibre
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M \neq 0$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a $\{p\}$-cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((q))$ obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise image of the function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L137) of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly, and let $j \in K$ be nonzero with image the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157). Let $k$ be an algebraically closed $A$-algebra field of characteristic $p$. Suppose $\mathrm{Gal}(L/\mathbb{Q}) = (L \simeq_{\mathbb{Q}} L)$ acts on $A$ by semiring automorphisms, compatibly with its action on $L$ along $A \to L$, and so that the induced maps on $k$ are trivial: $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,A\,k\,(s' \cdot a) = \mathrm{algebraMap}\,A\,k\,a$ for all $s'$, $a$. Write $X =$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChartModel A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L229), the pushout of the two morphisms of affine schemes induced by the inclusions of the $A$-subalgebras of $K$ generated by $j$, respectively by $j^{-1}$, into the middle chart, and let $\pi =$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) $: X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ be the morphism induced by the two structure maps. Given $s \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/\mathbb{Q})$ and endomorphisms $u, v$ of $X$ with $u$ followed by $\pi$ equal to $\pi$ followed by $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the action of $s$ on $A$, with $v$ satisfying the same relation for $s^{-1}$, and with $u \circ v$ and $v \circ u$ both the identity, the conclusion is that there is an automorphism $u_k$ of the fibre product $X \times_{\operatorname{Spec} A} \operatorname{Spec} k$ (taken along $\pi$ and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $A \to k$) such that $u_k$ followed by the first projection equals the first projection followed by $u$, $u_k$ followed by the second projection is the second projection, and $u_k^{-1}$ followed by the first projection equals the first projection followed by $v$.
--
--   This is the descent of a semilinear automorphism of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ over $A$ to an automorphism of its geometric special fibre over $k$, available because the Galois action becomes trivial after reduction to $k$. It supplies the special-fibre automorphisms used in the study of the Galois action on points of the special fibre of the two-chart model and of the associated Abel–Jacobi data.
